        "original_id": "6e9f9093-4d3a-5fbb-ab16-ca3591cf368a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Leslie Skinner\n- Products: Bazooka\n- Systems: shoulder-fired missiles, MANPADS, shoulder-launched surface-to-air missiles\n- Topics: rocket-propelled weapons, anti-tank weapons, infantry combat\n\nFacts:\n- During World War II, Leslie Skinner played a leading role in developing several rocket-propelled weapons.\n- During World War II, Leslie Skinner notably helped develop the Bazooka as the first shoulder-fired missile system.\n- The Bazooka was also referred to as the \"Stovepipe.\"\n- The Bazooka was among the first generation of rocket-propelled anti-tank weapons used in infantry combat.\n- The name \"Bazooka\" is often used informally for shoulder-fired missiles, although the actual Bazooka is a specific original shoulder-fired missile.\n- MANPADS, also called MPADS, are shoulder-launched surface-to-air missiles.",
